From: Gran Turismo 6 for Mac <https://github.com/Wooloomooloo2/Gran-Turismo-6-Mac>
Subject: [PATCH] lifter: guest setjmp/longjmp unwind the lifted host frames

Upstream: not yet submitted
Base: ps3recomp 4e8f3ca87a3e1d87bb83b8b7e9348fe2685cd514 (after 0001-0008)

What: new ppu_lifter options --setjmp EA[,EA] and --longjmp EA[,EA] name the
title's C library setjmp and longjmp. Every direct call to a setjmp becomes
PPU_SJLJ_SETJMP (runtime/ppu/ppu_sjlj.h): a host _setjmp into one element of
a zeroed frame array _sjf[N] declared at the top of the calling function,
registered per host thread and dropped on every return of that function
(ppu_sjlj_leave, by identity). The longjmp function, after its lifted body
has restored the guest registers, calls ppu_sjlj_longjmp, which
host-longjmps to the newest frame for the same jmp_buf, drops (and marks
unpushed) every newer frame, and puts back the indirect-call depth and
vcall stack the skipped frames held. Re-arming a call site unlinks only that
frame. With no frame for the buffer it logs and returns, as before. The
lifter warns when a --longjmp address is not a lifted function start. The
header states the invariant (no lifted C local may change between setjmp and
longjmp) and that jumping over a host HLE frame skips its destructors and
locks. The runtime half is in
ppu_loader.cpp (between guest-sjlj markers); the generated header includes
ppu_sjlj.h only when either option is given, so other lifts are unchanged.

Why: lifted, a guest longjmp only returned from the longjmp function; the
code after the call carried on with the registers of the setjmp. Gran
Turismo 6's file worker aborts a decode with longjmp when its consumer has
no output buffer left, so its inflater kept writing through a NULL or stale
buffer, overran a static buffer into its USB driver's state, and the game
exited on a failed mutex lock.

Test: tools/test_ppu_sjlj.py (new): the lifter rewrite, and the runtime with
stand-in lifted functions (landing value, skipped code, depth restore,
unknown and returned buffers, a re-armed call site, and two sites where a
longjmp to the first drops the second, the second is re-armed, and a longjmp
to the caller's buffer still lands).

